{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-008", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Midsummer shelves plans for solar cell factory in Sweden", "content": "<p>The Swedish solar manufacturer says it wants to focus on international expansion with a significantly less capital-intensive business and financing model for new factories.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/midsummer-shelves-plans-for-solar-cell-factory-in-sweden/\">Midsummer shelves plans for solar cell factory in Sweden</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/midsummer-shelves-plans-for-solar-cell-factory-in-sweden/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-009", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Negative prices reshape Europe’s solar, storage and PPA markets", "content": "<p>According to S&#38;P Global, rising negative electricity prices are reshaping solar, storage and PPAs across Europe. Wider price spreads are strengthening the case for batteries and more structured renewable energy ontracts.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/el-aumento-de-los-precios-negativos-redefine-las-senales-de-mercado-para-la-solar-el-almacenamiento-y-los-ppas-en-europa/\">Negative prices reshape Europe’s solar, storage and PPA markets</a> appeared first on", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/el-aumento-de-los-precios-negativos-redefine-las-senales-de-mercado-para-la-solar-el-almacenamiento-y-los-ppas-en-europa/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-010", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vehicle-integrated PV key to protecting EV batteries rather than extending range", "content": "<p>UK researchers say vehicle-integrated PV could deliver greater value by preserving EV batteries rather than extending driving range. Their review also calls for dynamic, automotive-specific testing standards that account for real-world shading, vehicle movement and module curvature.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/vehicle-integrated-pv-key-to-protecting-ev-batteries-rather-than-extending-range/\">Vehicle-integrated PV key to protecting EV batteries rather than e", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/vehicle-integrated-pv-key-to-protecting-ev-batteries-rather-than-extending-range/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-011", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "US startup develops drones to modify clouds, boost PV plant output by up to 30%", "content": "<p>US startup Meteoric Technologies is developing autonomous drones designed to modify clouds and increase solar radiation reaching PV plants. The company claims the technology could boost annual PV generation by 10% to 30%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/una-startup-estadounidense-desarrolla-drones-para-modificar-nubes-y-aumentar-hasta-un-30-la-produccion-de-plantas-fotovoltaicas/\">US startup develops drones to modify clouds, boost PV plant output by up to 30%</", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/una-startup-estadounidense-desarrolla-drones-para-modificar-nubes-y-aumentar-hasta-un-30-la-produccion-de-plantas-fotovoltaicas/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-012", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Ukraine auctions 150 MW of solar", "content": "<p>Ukraine will host two auctions, one for 50 MW of solar and another for 100 MW of solar-plus-storage, on September 25.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/ukraine-auctions-150-mw-of-solar/\">Ukraine auctions 150 MW of solar</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/ukraine-auctions-150-mw-of-solar/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-013", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.33, "keywords": ["increase", "overcapacity", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s solar module overcapacity pushes factory utilization to 35–40%", "content": "<p>India’s solar module manufacturing capacity has surged to 233 GW, outpacing domestic demand and pushing factory utilization down to 35–40%. A new IEEFA-JMK Research report warns that continued capacity additions could intensify pressure on margins and increase the risk of stranded assets.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/indias-solar-module-capacity-outpaces-demand-leaving-factories-running-at-just-35-40-utilization/\">India’s solar module overcapacity pushes fac", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/indias-solar-module-capacity-outpaces-demand-leaving-factories-running-at-just-35-40-utilization/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-014", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ATW unveils screen-printing solution for copper-metallized solar cell", "content": "<p>China’s Wuxi Autowell Technology has launched screen-printing equipment for copper and silver-coated copper pastes targeting TOPCon, back-contact, and next-generation solar cells. The product line includes cell-printing and print-on-print systems, as well as a curing furnace designed to prevent copper oxidation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/atw-unveils-screen-printing-solution-for-copper-metallized-solar-cell/\">ATW unveils screen-printing solution for copper", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/atw-unveils-screen-printing-solution-for-copper-metallized-solar-cell/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-015", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "New research confirms negligible LeTID degradation in TOPCon solar cells", "content": "<p>US researchers have found that light- and elevated-temperature-induced degradation (LeTID) has a limited impact on n-type TOPCon solar cells compared with earlier p-type PERC technology. Optimized firing conditions and laser-enhanced contact optimization (LECO) can further suppress degradation, with industrial TOPCon cells showing efficiency losses within acceptable warranty tolerances.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/new-research-confirms-negligible-letid-degr", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/new-research-confirms-negligible-letid-degradation-in-topcon-solar-cells/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-016", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Philippines to develop PV exemption areas", "content": "<p>Government officials in the Philippines are working to set boundaries between which lands can be used for solar projects and which should remain reserved for food production.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/philippines-to-develop-pv-exemption-areas/\">Philippines to develop PV exemption areas</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/philippines-to-develop-pv-exemption-areas/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-01-017", "date": "2026-09-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 36, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mexico’s CFE plans to deploy 5.4 GW of solar by 2030", "content": "<p>Mexico’s CFE plans MXN 651 billion ($32.9 billion) of investment through 2030, including 18.6 GW of new generation capacity, 82% of which it classifies as renewable.<br />\nThe program includes 5.48 GW of identified solar projects and mentions battery storage, although it sets no specific storage capacity or investment targets.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/mexicos-cfe-plans-to-deploy-5-4-gw-of-solar-by-2030/\">Mexico&#8217;s CFE plans to deploy 5.4 GW of solar", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/01/mexicos-cfe-plans-to-deploy-5-4-gw-of-solar-by-2030/", "type": "rss"}]}
